  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Facts",
      "items": [
        "Nothing is stored on disk: phone, seen and reports live in the Bridge node and go out whole on GET /api/state (bridge_node.py 454–461).",
        "phone and seen have no id of their own; they belong to whichever Link is current. opened() replaces both, closed() clears phone but leaves seen (bridge_node.py 305–318).",
        "Every value is checked and clamped by protocol.parse before it lands here.",
        "seen.camera also holds error and torch; codes keeps the last 5 read. Each sense records its time in at.",
        "Look adds two tables: what programs asked for (look, look/familiar) next to the facilitator's allowed, and the latest faces, each only x, y, size and a number (protocol.py 176–190).",
        "Since 0.5–0.6 the bridge also keeps what a phone that comes needs again (panel, see, an unanswered note), the phone's screen report for the mirrors, the show state with the last frame, and the programs' last states; opened() and closed() reset show and screen (bridge_node.py 305–318). A shown frame goes from Bridge.show to the loopback mirrors only (wsserver.py 225–231). Bridge.screen is the current phone's last report, and is cleared when it goes.",
        "Übersetzen (0.7) keeps no words: Translate holds whether it is allowed, the guest code and the last counts; each Session holds the utterance being heard, whose sound is dropped when its text is made (translate.py 217–255). The guest code is new each time Übersetzen is allowed (bridge_node.py 233–238)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Interpretation",
      "items": [
        "A report is matched to its phone by a random id the face and check pages keep in the browser (setup.js report()); by model only when storage is blocked. Until 9861131 it was by model alone, and one phone did not even match itself: hello named it from client hints, the report from the user agent (\"K\").",
        "The dicts are read by HTTP threads and written by the phone's thread without a lock. A stress test of json.dumps against a writer adding keys (200 000 runs, Python 3.12.3) raised no error: the values are replaced, not mutated.",
        "The id lives per address: the same phone has one id over USB (localhost) and another over Wi-Fi.",
        "A face's number reaches ROS only while familiar is both asked and allowed; otherwise the bridge sets it to null, whatever the phone sends (bridge_node.py 384–391). The signatures behind the numbers stay in the phone's page."
      ]
    }
  ]
